    "content": "\rD6_Table_1Table 1. Attrition table, one pair of columns (N, %) per datasource; saved as .docx, .html and .pdf. The same step creates D6_Figure_1_masked (.png, flowchart from excluded_counts_masked)\nD6_Figure_1_masked.png\rD6_Table_2_baseline_cohortTable 2. Patient Characteristics before imputation\nD6_Supplementary_Figure_1Supplementary Figure 1. Propensity score overlap by treatment group: histogram of the frequencies by bin, with the 1st and 99th percentile of each group as vertical lines; one PDF per datasource and subpopulation (D6_Supplementary_Figure_1_\u003cds\u003e.pdf, 10 x 8 inches)\nD6_Table_3_asd_before_after_weightingTable 3 Baseline characteristics of the study population overall and by treatment group (rivaroxaban vs apixaban), before and after IPTW\nD6_Table_S2_ORTable S2 Baseline characteristics of the study population by treatment group (rivaroxaban vs apixaban) and OR with 95% CI in the propensity score model\nD6_Table_4_follow_up_time_and_reasons_for_censoringTable 4. Follow-up time, intercurrent events, and reasons for censoring overall and by treatment group\nD6_Table_5_crude_IR_RMST\rD6_Table_S2_Crude_and_adjusted_differences_in_RMST\rD6_Table_6_HRTable 6. Crude and adjusted hazard ratios (95% CI) for estimands E1, E2 and crude and adjusted RMST for estimand E3a and E3b, masked\nD6_Table_8_SATable 8. Crude and adjusted hazard ratios (95% CI) for MACE comparing dapagliflozin with DPP-4 inhibitors across sensitivity analyses, CPRD\nD6_Table_10_TPTable 10. Best/worst case analysis showing the impact of varying assumptions about censoring on the estimated treatment effect; one table per datasource and subpopulation (.rds, .csv, .xlsx). Named D6_Table_10_SA in the index\nD6_Supplementary_Figure_2_MICESupplementary Figure 2. Propensity score overlap by treatment group in each of the 10 HbA1c-imputed datasets: one panel per imputation; one PDF per datasource and subpopulation (16 x 8 inches)\nD6_table_S3\rD6_Table_11_SA_MICETable 11. IPTW-adjusted hazard ratio of estimand 1 pooled over the 10 HbA1c-imputed datasets (Rubin's rules), one row per datasource and subpopulation\n ",
