    "content": "Documentation for the TARGET CS3 project _index.en\rSETTINGS\rSUBPOP\r_index.en\rcodelist_id_dataset\ritemset_id_dataset\r_index.enD3_PERSONScontains the cleaned version of PERSONS, where death date is reconstituted as date D3_OBSPERIODScontains the spells all the continuous spells of observation period of each person. in CPRD two versions of this dataset are generate, where the records are stratified per category: category_subpop = PC means that during the period the person is observed in primary care; category_subpop = PC_HOSP means that during the period the person is observed both in primary care and in hospital\n_index.en\rD3_STUDY_POPULATIONstudy population with their basic variables. _index.en\rD3_covariate_complex_IMPUTED_TD\rD3_EXP_ACT_COVstudy population with all covariates, before imputation D3_EXP_ACT_COV_IMPUTATIONstudy population with all covariates, after imputation D3_OUTCOMESOutcomes observed in the study population after t0 (\u003e t0), including setting that prompted the observation D5_DIAGNOSTIC_MEANING_OUTCOMES\rD5_DIAGNOSTIC_MEANING_OUTCOMES_masked\r_index.enD4_EXP_ACT_COV_WEIGHTexposed and comparators with covariates and weights D5_PS_model_OR\rD4_FUPexposed and comparators with follow-up time D5_check_recommended_end_date\rD5_check_recommended_end_date_masked\rD5_check_components_outcome\rD5_check_components_outcome_masked\rD4_EXP_ACT_COV_WEIGHT_TRUNCATEDexposed and comparators with covariates and weights, and truncated weights; records of persons with 0 weights are not included D4_ANALYTICAL_DATASET_HR_RMST_TPanalytical dataset with outcome indicator and follow-up time for each estimand (E1, E2, E3a, E3b) and for the tipping point analyses (TP1-TP4), used to compute incidence rates, hazard ratios and RMST D4_CENSORING_WEIGHTS_TRUNCATEDexposed and comparators with covariates and weights\n_index.enD5_Table_1Distribution and overlap of propensity scores by treatment group. A separate graph will be generated for the Finnish and UK database instances. D5_Table_2_baseline_cohortTable 2. Patient Characteristics D5_Supplementary_Figure_1Distribution and overlap of propensity scores by treatment group. D5_Table_3_asd_before_after_trimming\rD5_Table_4_follow_up_time_and_reasons_for_censoringTable 4. Follow-up time, intercurrent events, and reasons for censoring overall and by treatment group D5_table_S3\rD5_ResultsIR_HRResults of estimands and sensitivity analyses that use Incidence Rate and Cox model D5_ResultsRMSTnumber of persons and outcomes, person-years and incidence rates for E1, E2 and E3; crude and IPTW-adjusted restricted mean survival time (RMST) and its difference for E3 at 3 and 5 years\n_index.enD5_Table_1_maskedD5_Table_1 (attrition table) with counts between 1 and 4 masked; the same step also exports excluded_counts_masked, used for Figure 1 D5_Table_2_baseline_cohort_maskedD5_Table_2_baseline_cohort with counts between 1 and 4 masked; all variables are stored as character D5_Supplementary_Figure_1_maskeddistribution of the propensity score by treatment group, in bins of width 0.05, with frequencies between 1 and 4 masked D5_Table_3_asd_before_after_trimming_maskedD5_Table_3_asd_before_after_trimming with the unweighted counts (before weighting) between 1 and 4 masked; all variables are stored as character\n_index.enD6_Table_1Table 1. Attrition table, one pair of columns (N, %) per datasource; saved as .docx, .html and .pdf. The same step creates D6_Figure_1_masked (.png, flowchart from excluded_counts_masked) D6_Figure_1_masked.png\rD6_Table_2_baseline_cohortTable 2. Patient Characteristics before imputation D6_Supplementary_Figure_1Supplementary Figure 1. Propensity score overlap by treatment group: histogram of the frequencies by bin, with the 1st and 99th percentile of each group as vertical lines; one PDF per datasource and subpopulation (D6_Supplementary_Figure_1_\u003cds\u003e.pdf, 10 x 8 inches)\n ",
